## Summary

**Root cause:** In `llm/llama_server.go`, `memoryParsingWriter.updateRunnerMemoryLocked()` summed every reported buffer size into the process total. When a model is partially offloaded with mmap on, llama-server reports the weights *once per backend* (`CPU_Mapped model buffer` + `CUDA0/MTL0 model buffer`), but all of those mappings reference the same on-disk GGUF — so `ollama ps` counted the file-backed weights twice (e.g. ~26.6 GiB for a 13.26 GiB model).

**Fix:** In `updateRunnerMemoryLocked()`, track the model buffers that are file-backed (all `model` buffers except `_REPACK`, which are real copies). If their sum exceeds the actual model file size (via `os.Stat(runner.modelPath)`), subtract the excess from the reported total:

```go
if info, err := os.Stat(w.runner.modelPath); err == nil && info.Size() > 0 && fileBackedWeights > uint64(info.Size()) {
    total -= fileBackedWeights - uint64(info.Size())
}
```

The trim only touches the total — per-device VRAM (`memGPU`/`vramByDevice`) keeps the real GPU mapping sizes. Edge cases preserved: no trim when buffers fit within the file, when REPACK is the only overlap-free copy, when mmap is off, or when the file size is unknown.

`go test ./llm/...` → **ok**.
